<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13873" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποστομ-ᾰτίζω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στόμα</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>teach by word
				of mouth, teach by dictation,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γράμματα ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Euthd.</u>
					277a
				</span></i>
			: abs., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅταν ἀ. ὑμῖν ὁ
			γραμματεύς</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				276c
			</span></i>: —
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἀποστοματιζόμενον</span>
			<i>dictated lesson,</i> ibid., <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>SE</u>
				165b32
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>interrogate, catechize,</i> as a master his pupil, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
				11.53
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				1.102
			</span></i>(
				Pass.
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>repeat by heart,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				8.359d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antyll.
			</span></i> ap.<i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				6.9.4
			</span></i>: generally, <i>recite, repeat,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Thes.</u>
				24
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
